# Talk lines for the slice villagers that only exist in games that drew the storyline (T-143). Priority 2: above ordinary chat.

addto npc.wren.talk
2 storyline:pie_feud => wren.pie.1 cat=reactive tag=funny :: Marcus and Odalys are not speaking over a pie. I'm running a betting pool. Don't tell them.
2 storyline:pie_feud => wren.pie.2 cat=reactive :: The pie feud's day nine. The pie is still on the windowsill. Nobody dares touch it.
2 storyline:anonymous_notes => wren.notes.1 cat=reactive tag=funny :: Someone's leaving notes on doors. "Nice shoes," one said. I'm flattered. I wasn't wearing shoes.
2 storyline:anonymous_notes => wren.notes.2 cat=reactive :: I found a note that only said "Hello." It's the nicest thing that's happened this week.

addto npc.hazel.talk
2 storyline:pie_feud => hazel.pie.1 cat=reactive :: A pie, two neighbors. (I'm cataloguing the feud under "Domestic.") Nobody asked.
2 storyline:pie_feud => hazel.pie.2 cat=reactive :: The pie has gone stale. (The feud hasn't.) I find that instructive.
2 storyline:anonymous_notes => hazel.notes.1 cat=reactive :: Someone slipped a note into a book. (It said "Good choice.") I'm not sure which book.
2 storyline:anonymous_notes => hazel.notes.2 cat=reactive :: I think the notes are kind. (I'm trying not to look for the writer.) Looking spoils it.

addto npc.bram.talk
2 storyline:pie_feud => bram.pie.1 cat=reactive :: Hm. Pie feud. Two fools, one crust. I'd fix it with a hammer.
2 storyline:pie_feud => bram.pie.2 cat=reactive tag=funny :: Hm. Both sides asked me to make a pie plate. I made one. Gave it to Juno.
2 storyline:anonymous_notes => bram.notes.1 cat=reactive :: Hm. A note on my anvil. It said "Nice work." Hm. I read it twice.
2 storyline:anonymous_notes => bram.notes.2 cat=reactive :: Hm. I don't know who writes the notes. I'd like to say thanks.
